.TITLE "screencapture"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Captures screenshots and screen recordings on macOS. This command-line utility
offers extensive control over the screen capture process, allowing users to
capture the entire screen, a specific window, a selected area, or even record
video of screen activity. It supports various output formats and options.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**screenshot**

.DIV "TLDR"
**screencapture __screenshot.png__**
Captures the entire screen and saves it to a file named __screenshot.png__.
> __screenshot.png__: The output filename.

**screencapture -i __selection.png__**
Allows interactive selection of an area to capture and saves it to __selection.png__.
> __selection.png__: The output filename.

**screencapture -W __window.png__**
Captures a specific window interactively and saves it to __window.png__.
> __window.png__: The output filename.

**screencapture -T 5 __delayed.png__**
Captures the screen after a 5-second delay and saves it to __delayed.png__.
> __delayed.png__: The output filename.

**screencapture -C -P __clip.png__**
Captures the screen, includes the cursor, and copies the image to the clipboard, saving to __clip.png__.
> __clip.png__: The output filename.

.DIV "SUMMARY"
`screencapture` is a versatile tool for creating visual documentation or sharing
specific parts of your screen. Explore its many options (`man screencapture`)
to customize behavior like file format, shadow inclusion, and sound effects.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:sips**

